{"type": "result", "session_id": "20261005_133336_bdf14e", "exit_code": 0, "text": "No suitable matched mechanics/TEAD-to-start-output link exists in the audited GSE139321 inputs.\n\nThe native libraries cover cAMP/vehicle primary cultures, stable SOX10-knockout/parental S16 cells, and untreated adult nerves. There is no compression, matrix/stiffness, TEAD-perturbation or YAP/TAZ-genetic arm.\n\nOne qualification: PMC7430845 Par20 and Supplementary Figure 2B/C do validate Sox10 RNA/protein depletion in the knockout clones. That is perturbation validation—not a matched EGR2/SOX10 functional-activity or rescue endpoint under mechanical/TEAD perturbation. Likewise, Egr2/Sox10 RNA abundance and the nerve-derived chromatin overlaps cannot substitute for activity or occupancy measured in each cultured library.\n\nSeparate primary evidence does exist\n\nPMC5181599 contains:\n  Figure 4: Prom1/Prom2 first-exon RT-qPCR after Tead1 siRNA in rat primary and S16 cells.\n  Figure 5: first-exon RNA measurements under mouse Yap/Taz genetics at P3/P20.\n\nThose are relevant steady-state RNA endpoints under TEAD-pathway perturbation, but not mechanically perturbed, matched nascent/activity measurements linked to GSE139321. In Figure 5C, reduced Prom1 with nonsignificant Egr2 RNA change in P20 Taz cHet; Yap cKO nerve does not establish equivalent or restored EGR2 activity. The occupancy and reporter experiments remain separate; TEAD-motif mutations are reporter edits.\n\nExact existing evidence\n\nGSE139321 sample design:\nartifact_09517964b5420d7cc4239b33f2217718c240c81c9d943f3307b8ec0365f676e3\n\nPreserved PMC5181599 source:\nartifact_306fb5726176ef0cce72cbb8e050d575baedd023b6014e8fe674336b16a4c606\nProducer: post_c344fef84f344beca27925ec3f9ce940\n\nThe distinction is recorded and synced in LABBOOK. No new processing was performed, and the quantitative findings are unchanged.", "tokens": {"input": 20550, "output": 3362, "total": 782056, "cache_read": 758144, "cache_write": 0}, "dur